{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>I have become small from all the kindnesses.</b> I am too small to have all the kindnesses that You did with me come my way, and therefore I fear Esau, lest I not have merit in hand to escape him. Every expression of חסד ואמת has the sense of holding fast to goodness — from R. Yosef in la'az — as in 'ועשית עמדי חסד ואמת' (and do with me חסד ואמת), and as in 'שוב והשב את אחיך עמך חסד ואמת' (return and bring back your brother with you חסד ואמת), for it is written in connection with these." "<b>[And now I was.</b> I am.]"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The phrase מירצ״י בלע״ז is read as 'from R. Yosef (מר׳ יוסף) in la'az (לע״ז), i.e., a Romance vernacular gloss'; the final clause דגבי אתי הגתי is obscure and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:05.190482031Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}